<title>BELGIUM: Gevaert H1 net more than doubles.</title>
<headline>Gevaert H1 net more than doubles.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-08-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>First half to June 30, 1996</p>
<p>(in billion Belgian francs unless stated)</p>
<p>    Cons net profit				  3.769 vs 1.719</p>
<p>    Net earnings on capital transactions     2.246 vs 0.403</p>
<p>NOTE - Belgian holding company Gevaert NV said first half consolidated profiti was more than two billion francs higher due to a 14 percent increase in current income and a 1.8 billion franc rise in income from capital transactions.  </p>
<p>    Current income				   1.538 vs 1.350</p>
<p>    Profit per share (in francs)		   146 vs    67</p>
<p>NOTE - Gevaert said its estimated net asset value on June 30, 1996, was 2,455 francs against 2,245 francs on December 31, 1995 before dividend.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6815, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
